            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan Marie Rose"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Amazing. You never would have guessed that this is made from tofu. I made a macaroni salad with it and served it at the company picnic. Not a single person guessed that it was a non-dairy mayo. Great for my family who have severe dairy allergies"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pryceless"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Incredible!! I used dijon instead of dry mustard and added paprika, garlic powder and lemon juice. I didn't measure; just sort of eye-balled the extra additions. I let it sit in the refrigerator for a couple hours and served with the Fruity Chicken Salad and Quick biscuits from this site. Wonderful saturday afternoon meal.",
            "datePublished": "2008-08-30T07:46:02.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "neo7754"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe yesterday and it was much better than I thought it would be. I used lemon juice instead of vinegar. I used a medium tofu and next time I would use the firm. I am going to play with this recipe and spices until I get it just right for me. Thank You.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-19T08:39:58.597Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe! I added 2 garlic cloves and a little bottled lemon juice and I used dijon mustard instead of mustard powder. I also added an egg yolk because I like a slight eggy taste in my mayo. I WILL DEFINITELY MAKE IT AGAIN! It's probably even creamier when the tofu is frozen first, then defrosted.",
            "datePublished": "2004-06-26T10:30:55.000Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Natasha Buel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "For those who are unfamiliar with vegetarian/vegan cooking this will not taste like traditional mayo. However, this has been one of the best tofu mayo I've had next to the store bought. The only change I made, like some of the other reviewers, is to substitute brown mustard for the dry mustard. I saved this recipe and I feel it is definitely worth trying!",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-07T13:23:56.347Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "karaleefc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i used dijon mustard instead of mustard powder. it tasted little bland for my taste but after adding about a tsp of lemon juice me and my fam ADORED it.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-28T22:42:31.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WLDKATFAN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is yummy!!! I used lemon juice instead of vinegar and added a little garlic powder. This is definatly a keeper :-)",
            "datePublished": "2001-10-31T13:34:38.983Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this recipe didn't taste like mayo...just tasted like tofu. So, i decided to revise it a little to make it taste like mayo. i looked at the ingredients for actual mayo and i added cream cheese, garlic, paprika, lemon juice and more salt. Pretty soon it tasted more like mayo. \r\nNice try on the recipe though.",
            "datePublished": "2002-10-05T12:49:44.407Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Claas Daughter"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Followed recipe exactly, but found it to be flavorless. Consistency was a little more liquid than mayo, but within reason for a substitute. Used it for tuna salad, so lack of flavor did not matter as much.",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-15T02:40:11.312Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "John Dayton"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used prepared brown mustard instead of dry and followed the recipe otherwise. This \"mayo\" is a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-28T12:53:35.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jake"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was pleasantly surprised with this. As with most \"alternative\" recipes, I was not expecting identical taste. That being said, it was quite good. (I followed the original recipe.) After tasting, I used it in a chicken salad where mixed with other flavors no one had a clue it wasn't egg/oil based store-bought mayo. Only after it was entirely consumed did I reveal that it was tofu. Several folks wanted the recipe. I'll be using this in future endeavours.",
            "datePublished": "2013-09-26T12:16:07.950Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RIVERSPEACE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My first thought was, if it is really that easy and that tasty, why doesn't everyone make tofu mayo? After tasting it my thought was, why the heck have I not been making this for years. I am not vegetarian but I like it better than regular mayo!",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-23T10:48:44.573Z"
